  "id": "COMPOUND:3095 - PROTEIN:6020",
  "verbalization": "Isoliquiritigenin appears to interact with PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1 through a series of target relationships, with the most direct link being through the UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10 enzyme. This enzyme is a target of Isoliquiritigenin and also of other compounds like Sennoside D and Acetamide, all of which ultimately target the same kinase. The presence of multiple compounds with similar target profiles suggests a potential mechanism involving the modulation of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10, which may influence the activity of PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1. The evidence supports a pathway where Isoliquiritigenin could either directly or indirectly affect the kinase through its interaction with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10, potentially altering its function or signaling pathways. The integration of these findings highlights a possible role for Isoliquiritigenin in modulating the activity of this kinase, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
